verdicts.recommended_fix:
1. **Copper.** Add a stage to r7_polish, or to the R6 inheritance step, that deletes QSPI_IO3's five F.Cu segments: (22.5,40.3)–(22.5,37.7), (22.5,37.7)–(21.3,37.7), (21.3,37.7)–(21.3,36.7), (21.3,36.7)–(22.5,36.7) and (22.5,36.7)–(22.5,35.4). Replace them with one segment (22.5,40.3)→(22.5,35.4), F.Cu, 0.2 mm wide. Then rebuild with r7_build.sh and rerun tools/check.sh and the tests. I verified this edit on a scratch copy: DRC, parity, route_check, check_r7, check_actuators and critical_reference are all clean, and GND F.Cu gains 1.9 mm².

2. **Records.**
- Correct R7_VALIDATION part F. Local detours on critical nets are M2 review items, because route_check's detour test works per net, not locally.
- Record the judgement for each remaining critical-net chain detour:
  - the radio corridor Z-routes: their A/B entries or the measured strip constraints;
  - PYRO1_CONT's U-turn round R130.2;
  - ARM1_SENSE: an L;
  - USB_DM/DP: the USB-C A6/B6/A7/B7 crossover;
  - QSPI_IO2's In2 overshoot near (32.5,57.7): ties to allowlist entry A for extra vias;
  - SPI1_SCK's hook into U4.
- List any instance that remains under "R7 deviations for owner acceptance". Deal with this together with P6-DOCS-01.

